hume-enquiry-4.logic.r2: argue/answered: U1: answered yes, which keeps hume-enquiry-4.logic.r2, to: Does the text's argument take this for granted, whether or not it says so: "if it is a principle of reason that all sensible qualities are in the mind, not in the object, then matter is bereaved of all its intelligible qualities, both primary and secondary"? Answer yes if the author would accept it as part of the argument.
