hume-enquiry-4.logic.r2: argue/answered: U2: answered yes, which keeps hume-enquiry-4.logic.r2, to: Does the text's argument take this for granted, whether or not it says so: "if matter is in a manner annihilated, leaving only a certain unknown, inexplicable something as the cause of our perceptions, then the opinion of external existence is contrary to reason"? Answer yes if the author would accept it as part of the argument.
